CBraMod embeddings and fine-tuning heads read the output of its encoder, as in the authors' fine-tuning code, instead of `proj_out`, the head that reconstructs masked patches in pretraining: CBraMod embeddings change, so extract them again. The head of a linear probe on LaBraM reads the mean of its patch tokens, the vector its embeddings hold, instead of the [CLS] token, which neither pretraining nor the authors' fine-tuning read.
